  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\n- Dry through Saturday Morning\n\nDry weather is forecast from this afternoon right through Saturday\nmorning. High pressure will dominate the Great Lakes weather\nthrough that time. BUFKIT overviews show very little moisture\nthrough the depth of the atmosphere outside of limited cumulus\nlevel moisture (4-7k feet). Temperatures will be comfortable as\nwill humidity levels. Highs will be in the 70s to near 80 the \nnext two days with lows mainly in the 50s.\n\n- Chances for Showers and Storms Beginning Saturday Evening\n\nThe weather pattern becomes more active Saturday evening into\nearly next week as a northwest upper flow moves shortwaves \nthrough the region. A stronger wave looks to move through Saturday\ninto Saturday night with additional waves continuing into early \nnext week. Machine learning schemes are picking up on Sunday and \nMonday being two of the more active weather days with a warm front\nin the area and fairly deep moisture given PWATs in the 1.50 to\n2.00 range. Stronger winds through the profile also aid the \npossibilities of severe weather with deep layer shear values\nincreasing to 40-50+ knots. Right now our 7 day forecast QPF is \nunder a half inch but could see this needing to be nudged upward\nwith time.\n\n- Heat Builds into the Weekend\n\n850mb temperatures tonight will be around +9C. These temperatures\nwill increase into the weekend with +20C or higher expected from\nSunday into Tuesday. Sunday and Monday look to be the warmest days\nwith highs pushing to around 90F.",
